1,0 $ ===> Retour au kit$$f"Phaeocollybia_Kit.cle"
1,0 $ Spores smooth s.m. (faintly ornamented SEM) $ Stagnicola perplexa
1,2 $ Spores distinctly ornamented

2,0 $ Marginal cystidia with long neck surmounted by capitate apex; $ Ph. lugubris
2,0,N$ Synonyme : Naucoria lugubris (Fr.) QuéI. in Suppl. 10, Champg. Jura Vosges 3 (663), 1880./// ICONOGRAPHIE:///- Bresadola. 791; ///- Cooke. 1169 (1187);///- Ricken 529, figs;///- Brittonia 9: 210,1957, figs 24 and 25;///- Beit. Crypt. Suisse 13: 566,1968;///- Windhalia 12-13: 65,1983, fig. 2.
2,0,N$ cap clay buff to ochraceous darkening to rust or rusty tawny with age; gills pallid to olivaceous buff then ochraceous, finally fulvous spotted with rust-colour
2,3 $ Marginal cystidia clavate to elongate cylindric with or without capitate apex

3,0 $  Spores 7-9.5/4-5(-5.5) µm; cap olivaceous becoming buff with citrine tinge to isabeIIine spotted rusty tawny $ Ph. festiva
3,0,N$ Synonymes : Naucoria festiva (Fr.) Bres., Fungi Tridentini I: 19,1882.///ICONOGRAPHIE :///- Bresadola 792;///- Bresadola FT 1:22;///- Cooke. 1170 (966);///- FRIC (1972). Plate 48C. Figs:///- Brittonia 9: 210, 1957, fig. 30;///- Windhalia 12-13: 69,1983, fig. 4.
3,4 $ Spores smaller, never greater than 6.5 µm; cap lacking olivaceous tints

4,0 $ Marginal cystidia narrowly cylindric, non-capitate sometimes flexuose; cap not striate $ Ph. jennyi
4,0,N$///Synonymes :Naucoria jennyi Karsten in Hedwigia20: 178,1881./// Misident.: Phaeocollybia cidaris (Fr.) Heim sensu Kuhner in Bull. Soc. Nat. d'Oyonnax 10-11, Suppl.: 48, 1957 non Agaricus cidaris Fries.///ICONOGRAPHIE:///- Fr. 123/2, cidaris var. minor. Figs: Kühner, I.c., 48, fig. 23, 1957;///- Bon, Doc. Mycol. 21(84), 45 with fig., 1992.
4,0 $ Marginal cystidia elongate cylindric, usually capitate apex; cap striate at margin $ Ph. arduennensis
4,0,N$///Misident.: Phaeocollybia jennyi (Karst.) Heim ss. Dennis, Orton & Hora, 1960; Naucoria jennyi Karst. ss. Pears on 1952 and Lange, 1938.///ICONOGRAPHIE: Lange 123-A (sub nom. Naucoria jennyae).///
